en.fuller:
μιμνήσκω
(Bl., -ῄ-, § 3, 3), [in LXX chiefly for זָכַר ;]
to remind: mid, and pass.;
__(a) reflexive, to remind oneself of, hence, to remember: with genitive of thing(s), Mat.26:75, Luk.1:54, 72 24:8, Act.11:16, 2Pe.3:2, Ju 17; with neg., of sins, = to forgive, Heb.8:12 10:17" (LXX) ; with genitive of person(s), Luk.23:42; before ὅτι, Mat.5:23 27:63, Luk.16:25, Jhn.2:17, 22 12:16; ὡς, Luk.24:6; pf., μέμνημι, in Pres. sense (cl.), with genitive of person(s) (of thing(s)), 1Co.11:2, 2Ti.1:4; pres., μιμνήσκομαι (only in late writers), with genitive of person(s), in sense of caring for, Heb.2:6 (LXX) Heb.13:3;
__(b) in passive sense, to be remembered, aor., ἐμνήσθην : before ἐνώπιον, with genitive of person(s) (cf. Eze.18:22), Act.10:31, Rev.16:19 (cf. ἀνα-, ἐπ-ανα-, ὑπο- μιμνήσκω. The tenses of this verb are from the older μνάομαι).†
(AS)

es.fuller:
μιμνήσκω
(Bl., -ῄ-, § 3, 3), [en LXX princ. for זָכַר ;]
to remind: mid, and pas.;
(a) reflexive, to remind oneself of, hence, to remember: con gen. de cosa, Mt.26:75, Lc.1:54, 72 24:8, Hch.11:16, 2P.3:2, Jud  17; con neg.., of sins, = to forgive, Heb.8:12 10:17" (LXX) ; con gen. de pers., Lc.23:42; before ὅτι, Mt.5:23 27:63, Lc.16:25, Jn.2:17, 22 12:16; ὡς, Lc.24:6; pf., μέμνημι, in Pres. sense (clás.), con gen. de pers. (of thing(s)), 1Co.11:2, 2Ti.1:4; pres., μιμνήσκομαι (only in late writers), con gen. de pers., in sense of caring for, Heb.2:6 (LXX) Heb.13:3;
(b) in passive sense, to be remembered, aor., ἐμνήσθην : before ἐνώπιον, con gen. de pers. (cf. Ez.18:22), Hch.10:31, Ap.16:19 (cf. ἀνα-, ἐπ-ανα-, ὑπο- μιμνήσκω. The tenses of this verb are from the older μνάομαι).†
(AS)

he.fuller:
μιμνήσκω
(Bl., -ῄ-, § 3, 3), [בשבעים בעיקר for זָכַר ;]
to remind: mid, and סביל;
(a) reflexive, to remind oneself of, hence, to remember: עם יחס׳ של דבר, מתי.26:75, לוקס.1:54, 72 24:8, מע״ש.11:16, 2פ.3:2, יהו  17; עם שלילה., of sins, = to forgive, עב.8:12 10:17" (LXX) ; עם יחס׳ של אדם, לוקס.23:42; before ὅτι, מתי.5:23 27:63, לוקס.16:25, יוחנן.2:17, 22 12:16; ὡς, לוקס.24:6; pf., μέμνημι, in Pres. sense (קלאסית), עם יחס׳ של אדם (of thing(s)), 1קור.11:2, 2טי.1:4; pres., μιμνήσκομαι (only in late writers), עם יחס׳ של אדם, in sense of caring for, עב.2:6 (LXX) עב.13:3;
(b) in passive sense, to be remembered, עבר, ἐμνήσθην : before ἐνώπιον, עם יחס׳ של אדם (השוו יח.18:22), מע״ש.10:31, התג.16:19 (השוו ἀνα-, ἐπ-ανα-, ὑπο- μιμνήσκω. The tenses of this verb are from the older μνάομαι).†
(AS)

en.fuller:
μονή, -ῆς, ἡ
(μένω), [in LXX: 1Ma.7:38 * ;]
__1. in cl.,
__(a) a staying, abiding;
__(b) continuance (LXX, 1 with)
__2. In late Gk.,
__(a) a statson (Paus.);
__(b) an abode: Jhn.14:2, 23;
__(with) a monastery (cf. MM, iii, xvi; so in MGr.).†
(AS)

